\section*{Compilation Instructions}
To compile the thesis into a fully typeset PDF, run the standard LaTeX 
four-pass sequence in your local environment:

\begin{verbatim}
pdflatex thesis_300_pages.tex
bibtex thesis_300_pages
pdflatex thesis_300_pages.tex
pdflatex thesis_300_pages.tex
\end{verbatim}

\subsection*{Compilation Notes}
\begin{itemize}
    \item The first \texttt{pdflatex} pass generates auxiliary files.
    \item \texttt{bibtex} processes citations and bibliography entries.
    \item The second and third \texttt{pdflatex} passes resolve references,
          floats, lists of figures/tables, and cross-links.
    \item Ensure that all figure paths in \texttt{thesis\_300\_pages.tex} 
          match the directory structure shown above.
\end{itemize}

